{"id": "haiku__GEN__omni_2293__0", "result": "**Answer: 168089**\n\n**Reduction.** A positive integer is divisible by some cube greater than 1 exactly when it is divisible by $p^3$ for some prime $p$. So the count is $N - Q(N)$, where $N = 999999$ and $Q(N)$ is the number of cube-free integers in $[1, N]$.\n\n**Counting cube-free integers.** By M\u00f6bius inversion,\n$$Q(N) = \\sum_{d\\ge 1} \\mu(d)\\left\\lfloor \\frac{N}{d^3}\\right\\rfloor,$$\nand only $d \\le 99$ contribute since $100^3 > N$.\n\n**Positive terms** ($\\mu(d)=+1$, floor values in parentheses):\n$d=1$ (999999), 6 (4629), 10 (999), 14 (364), 15 (296), 21 (107), 22 (93), 26 (56), 33 (27), 34 (25), 35 (23), 38 (18), 39 (16), 46 (10), 51 (7), 55 (6), 57 (5), 58 (5), 62 (4), 65 (3), 69 (3), 74 (2), 77 (2), 82 (1), 85 (1), 86 (1), 87 (1), 91 (1), 93 (1), 94 (1), 95 (1).\n\nSum: $1{,}006{,}707$.\n\n**Negative terms** ($\\mu(d)=-1$):\n$d=2$ (124999), 3 (37037), 5 (7999), 7 (2915), 11 (751), 13 (455), 17 (203), 19 (145), 23 (82), 29 (41), 30 (37), 31 (33), 37 (19), 41 (14), 42 (13), 43 (12), 47 (9), 53 (6), 59 (4), 61 (4), 66 (3), 67 (3), 70 (2), 71 (2), 73 (2), 78 (2), 79 (2), 83 (1), 89 (1), 97 (1).\n\nSum: $174{,}797$.\n\nTerms with $\\mu(d)=0$ (non-squarefree $d$) contribute nothing.\n\nSo $Q(N) = 1{,}006{,}707 - 174{,}797 = 831{,}910$.\n\n**Check.** The cube-free density is $1/\\zeta(3) \\approx 0.83191$, and $0.83191 \\times 999999 \\approx 831{,}906$, which agrees with $831{,}910$.\n\n**Result.**\n$$999999 - 831910 = 168089.$$\n\nANSWER: 168089", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.00279622, "model_used": ["claude-haiku-5-5"], "secs": 26.7}